# References between fields (UnitInput: `{` picks, chips, ƒ, → N, cycle error, part menu, broken reference).
# `cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/references.drive out/references`
viewport 1280x1100
scale 1

# Select the fin set in Station Lanes.
click (922, 924)
screenshot 01-fins.png

# Height: type `0.5 * {` -- pick mode. The field gets the accent ring, the other numeric fields dashed accent outlines.
click (1180, 323)
type "0.5 * {"
screenshot 02-pick-mode.png

# Click the Root chord field: it lands as a chip. Keep typing maths around it.
click (1180, 255)
screenshot 03-chip.png
type " + 2"
screenshot 04-chip-maths.png

# Enter commits: the result with the ƒ badge (0.5 x 120 + 2 = 62 mm); Root chord shows → 1.
type enter
screenshot 05-committed.png

# Change the source: Height follows (50 mm).
click (1180, 255)
type "100"
type enter
screenshot 06-source-changed.png

# A cycle: Root chord may not use Height, which uses Root chord.
click (1180, 255)
type "{"
click (1180, 323)
type enter
screenshot 07-circular.png

# Click a part in Station Lanes during a pick: its value menu opens (Tip chord = 2 x {Body tube, ...}).
click (1180, 343)
type "2 * {"
click (870, 896)
screenshot 08-part-menu.png

# Pick "Outer Ø" of the Body tube from the menu: it lands as a chip with the part's system colour.
click (910, 947)
screenshot 09-menu-picked.png
type enter
screenshot 10-part-formula.png

# Hovering a formula field shows the formula.
move (1180, 289)
screenshot 11-hover-formula.png

# Scrubbing a formula field asks first (grip of Tip chord).
click (1100, 289)
screenshot 12-scrub-asks.png
click "Cancel"

# Source side: Root chord shows → 1; click it to list the dependants.
click (1224, 255)
screenshot 13-dependants.png
click (1224, 255)


# Sweep length takes a value of the ballast, picked in Station Lanes (the menu slides back inside the window).
click (1180, 357)
type "0.5 * {"
click (510, 1029)
screenshot 14-ballast-menu.png
click (550, 1045)
type enter
screenshot 15-ballast-formula.png

# Delete the ballast: the reference breaks. The chip turns red and struck through; the value is kept.
click (510, 1029)
click (1257, 62)
click "Delete"
click (922, 924)
screenshot 16-broken.png
click "Re-pick"
screenshot 17-broken-chip.png
type escape
click "Convert"
screenshot 18-converted.png
